\description{
ggplot2 allows \code{limits} to be a function, but only passes it the value
range (min/max) — not enough for quantiles. These subclasses therefore
remember the trained values in \code{train()} and compute the quantiles from
them in \code{get_limits()}. This has to go through \verb{super =} rather than
overriding individual methods after the fact: ggplot2 clones scales when
building the plot (\code{Scale$clone()}), and only real ggproto methods then
bind to the cloned object.
}
